Subject: [PATCH 88/94] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: Add the CPU memory paths

Give every CPU its path from the application processor to DDR, the
same APSS -> EBI path the CPU BWMON votes on and downstream's
cpufreq-mapped mincpubw client used (msm_bus ports 1 -> 512).
qcom-cpufreq-hw then votes the opp-peak-kBps of the OPP a cluster
switches to, so a board whose CPU OPP tables carry bandwidths gets a
DDR floor per CPU frequency.

The vote is active-only, as downstream's qcom,active-only: it is
dropped from the RPM's sleep set and never keeps DDR up while the
application processor is power collapsed.

The CPU devices set only of_node, so fw_devlink creates no device
links for them, and the interconnect providers' sync_state does not
wait on CPUs, which never bind a driver.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
